        p#par0220 Calculated emissions are analyzed from different points of view:
        p#par0225
            | A) According to the whether the pollutants affect climate change, air quality or health, they were classified as: i) greenhouse gases (CO
            sub 2
            | , CH
            sub 4
            |  and N
            sub 2
            | O) grouped as CO
            sub 2
            | eq (weighted by their global potential warming); ii) ozone precursors (linear sum of CO, NOX and VOC) and iii) impacting air quality (linear sum of PM10, PM2.5 and SO
            sub 2
            | ). Greenhouse gases were calculated according to their global warming potential, converting them to CO2eq; while emissions of ozone precursors and air quality were added in equal proportion.
        p#par0230
            | B) According to the generating sector, that is, where emissions are produced, we organized the emissions in four subgroups: i) production of electricity, ii) transport, iii) residential and commercial, iv) transformation in refineries and cement production (
