    section
        h3.top#sec0115 Spatial comparison with EDGAR
        p#par0260
            | To evaluate uncertainty in the spatial distribution, we compared the inventory here proposed (GEAA) with the EDGAR international database, which is often used in those areas for which there are not any specific national inventories.
        p#par0265
            | We compared the road transportation and residential sectors since they are widely distributed in the territory. Due to different resolutions (GEAA is 4 times finer), we converted the GEAA data to the EDGAR resolution, adding 16 GEAA-cells included in each EDGAR cell (hereinafter called “low resolution”). Additionally, the reverse conversion was done by adapting EDGAR data to the GEAA resolution, dividing each cell by 16 and repeating the same value in the 16 cells (hereinafter called “high resolution”). As can be observed in
            a(href='#tbl0065') Table 12
            | , the total values for Argentina in both inventories for these subsectors are very similar. However, the spatial distribution of these values shows important discrepancies. In
            a(href='#fig0070') Fig. 14
            | , blue colors indicate higher EDGAR values and red colors show higher GEAA values.
